   "subject": "Re: Fully standardized EPC larger than 6",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">So the fully standardized EPC statistic is 5 times larger than the latents-only standardized EPC statistic. Do you have one observed variable whose variance is disproportional to the variances of the others? That can cause SEM methods to misbehave. Also, your modification index of 240 is pretty large, so the estimate of EPC may be more approximate. That is, relaxing that constraint could lead to very dramatic change in your parameter estimates, and it would be a lot to ask that EPC or standardized EPC nailed the change in this one parameter estimate.</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
